# November 19, 2026: Broome County, New York (Binghamton, Johnson City, Endicott, Endwell, Chenango Forks, Ouaquaga,
# Hawleyton). Drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny (region scho), which offered Jefferson, Binghamton and
# Johnson City; the Atlas had nothing within 20 km of Binghamton. The Triple Cities' standing landmarks (Isaac Perry's
# asylum and mansion, the courthouse, the old city hall, two bluestone Episcopal churches, the DL&W station), George F.
# Johnson's six carousels and the Square Deal Arch, two lenticular truss bridges, and Lock 107 of the Chenango Canal.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py, including the Broome County Register list),
# HMdb marker pages, Broome County's carousel page, the Village of Johnson City and Village of Endicott parks pages, the
# Town of Union's carousel history page, the Phelps Mansion's tours page, the Roberson Museum's visit page, Trinity
# Memorial Church's home page, the Bundy Museum's home page, New York State Parks' Chenango Valley page, the Town of
# Fenton's Chenango Canal page, WICZ (Christ Church), WNBF (the Johnson City arch, 2025-2026).
from data_b import N
